# The findings of tools/verify/suitecheck.sh in the tests that predate etude's
# case manifests, one line per file and rule as FILE: COUNT RULE. The rules are
# `sleep`, a sleep that waits for no event; `bound`, an upper bound on a
# duration; and `skip`, a line that prints a skip in a test that passes. A
# conversion to etude's cases (dev-log/62-etude/plan.md) declares each in a
# case's timing or removes it. A file whose count differs from its entry fails
# the check, so the list only falls. A person reads this list.
